@flexiarg snatch/ask-for-surplus-not-surrender
@title Ask for Surplus, Not Surrender
@audience players
@tone practical
@style pattern
@why snatch/exchange-when-both-sides-gain
@see-also snatch/probe-before-committing

! conclusion: Pair what you give with a non-zero ask that preserves a gain for both players.

  + context: **Play grain.** P1 is composing an offer while both players retain
    tokens that the other values more highly.

  + IF:
    You are offering a positive number of your tokens and may still choose what
    to ask in return.

  + HOWEVER:
    Choosing only the give side turns an exchange into a transfer, while an ask
    that consumes the counterpart's entire benefit gives acceptance no reason.

  + THEN:
    Ask for at least one token, and keep the pair inside the range where
    acceptance produces positive value for each side.

  + BECAUSE:
    The ask is half the offer's payoff. Naming it makes the proposed mutual gain
    explicit instead of treating P2's contribution as an afterthought.
